# Input
```svelte
<!-- should generate diagnostics -->
<script>
	import { writable } from "svelte/store";

	const user = writable(null, async (set) => {
		set(await fetchUser());
	});
</script>

<p>{$user}</p>

```

# Diagnostics
```
invalid.svelte:5:30 lint/nursery/noSvelteAsyncStore ━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━

  i This async function is passed to writable().
  
    3 │ 	import { writable } from "svelte/store";
    4 │ 
  > 5 │ 	const user = writable(null, async (set) => {
      │ 	                            ^^^^^
    6 │ 		set(await fetchUser());
    7 │ 	});
  
  i Svelte calls the value this function returns when the store is no longer used. An async function returns a promise, and calling a promise throws an error.
  
  i Make the function synchronous, start the async work inside it, and call set() when the result is ready.
  
  i This rule belongs to the nursery group, which means it is not yet stable and may change in the future. Visit https://biomejs.dev/linter/#nursery for more information.
  

```
